## Costs (AWS)

| Resource | Instance | Approx Cost/Month |
|----------|----------|-------------------|
| EC2 t3.medium | 24/7 | ~$30 USD |
| Elastic IP (when attached) | Free | $0 |
| Data transfer (first 100GB) | Free tier | $0 |
| Supabase (free tier) | — | $0 |
| Redis Cloud (free 30MB) | — | $0 |
| Gemini API (free quota) | — | $0 |

> **Tip:** Use a `t3.small` (~$15/mo) if you're low on budget — it may be slower but will work.

---

## Common Issues

| Error | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY is required` | Set `GEMINI_API_KEY` in `.env` on EC2 |
| Container keeps restarting | Run `docker compose logs <service-name>` to see the error |
| Port 80 not accessible | Check Security Group inbound rules allow port 80 |
| CORS error in browser | Add your EC2 IP/domain to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `.env` and restart |
| `docker: permission denied` | Run `sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu` then logout/login |
| DB connection failed | Check `DATABASE_URL` format — use Supabase Session Pooler URL |
